+4. **Sources.** Count sources used with specific, accurate details (of four), and how many details per source. Three or four sources with several specifics each is a strong sign. Explicit source labels such as "(Source 2)" attached to evidence inside advantage paragraphs are a sign of deliberate, organized source use. Thin use (one or two details per source) is weak even if all four are named. Minor factual slips and some misreadings cost little; do not drop an essay a full level just for them unless the source content is mostly garbled.
